.TH "OSTRYA\-COMPOSEFS\-IMAGE" "1" "" "ostrya" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ostrya\-composefs\-image \- Write the composefs image of a commit as an image commit
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
ostrya composefs\-image [OPTIONS] \-\-add <REV>
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Write the composefs image of a commit as an image commit.
.PP
\%\-\-add writes the image commit of a commit and names it as the supplement \fB\%composefs\fR of the commit. The option is required.
.PP
The command prints nothing on success. If the action fails, the command writes one \fB\%error:\fR line to standard error and exits \%1. This command is an extension of ostrya.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-add\fR \fIREV\fR
Write the image commit of the commit REV, and name it as the supplement \fB\%composefs\fR of REV.
.IP
The command refuses a commit that names an image commit as the attachment \fB\%composefs\fR\&. If the supplement \fB\%composefs\fR names a valid image commit, the command does nothing. Else the command builds the image of the tree, writes the image commit, and sets the supplement \fB\%composefs\fR of REV to it. This replaces an entry that names another image commit, an image commit that the repository does not hold or holds partial, or an image commit whose tree has a defect.
.IP
The command does not write again an object that the repository already holds. If the entry names the image commit that the build gives, and the object of its \fB\%/root.cfs\fR is changed on disk, the command writes the same entry and exits \%0, and the changed object stays. A changed object is a defect that \fB\%fsck\fR reports.
.IP
If REV carries \fB\%ostree.composefs.digest.v0\fR and the \%fs\-verity digest of the built image is not the value of the key, the command refuses REV and names both digests. If REV has no key, the command makes no check. A refusal writes no object and no supplement. The command works in each repository mode. It does not refuse a partial commit, and the build fails if an object of the tree is absent.
.IP
No transfer copies a supplement. A pull of REV copies its detached metadata, and not the image commit.
.PP
The global options are listed in \fBostrya\fR(1).
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBostrya\fR(1)
